  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Evaluating limits of functions (d)</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Evaluate the value of the following limit:</p>

<p>\(\displaystyle \lim_{x\rightarrow {@var_limit@}} \frac{\sin( {@var_1@}\pi)}{x} =\)[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]][[feedback:prt1]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked solution</h3>

[[ if test='var_limit = 0' ]]
  <p>\(\displaystyle f(x)=  \frac{\sin( {@var_1@}\pi)}{x} ,\) is undefined at \(x={@var_limit@}\).</p>

[[ else ]]
   <p>To evaluate the limit</p> <p>\(\displaystyle \lim_{x\rightarrow {@var_limit@}} \frac{\sin( {@var_1@}\pi)}{x} \)</p>
<p>We first need to calculate \(\displaystyle  \frac{\sin( {@var_1@}\pi)}{x} \)</p>
<p>Notice that  \(  {@var_1 @}\pi \) radians is equivalent to \({@decimalplaces(var_1,1)@} \pi ,\) which corresponds to \({@decimalplaces((var_1*180),0)@}\) in degrees</p>
<p>The sine function's periodicity means that  \(\displaystyle \sin {@decimalplaces(var_1,1)@} \pi =\sin {@float(var_1-2)@}\pi= {@eqn_1@}\)</p>
<p>Now substitute this value into the limit:</p><p>\(\displaystyle \lim_{x\rightarrow {@var_limit@}} \frac{\sin( {@var_1@}\pi)}{x} = \frac{{@eqn_1@}}{{@var_limit@}}={@ta@}\) </p>
[[/ if]]]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
